{% doc %}
  Prints a merchant's text setting when it has one, HTML-escaped, and otherwise the storefront
  translation for `key` in the visitor's language. Shopify's t filter escapes its own output, so
  neither branch escapes twice, and the result is safe in element text and attribute values alike.

  @param {string} [value] - The text setting's value; blank falls back to the translation.
  @param {string} key - A storefront translation key, such as nubandina.coffee_finder.heading.

  @example
  {% render 'nubandina-text', value: section.settings.heading, key: 'nubandina.coffee_finder.heading' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- if value != blank -%}{{ value | escape }}{%- else -%}{{ key | t }}{%- endif -%}
